      "id": "sol.ahsme-1956-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Substituting \\(x=2,\\) and evaluating the exponent first, gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} x+x(x^x)&=2+2(2^2)\\\\ &=2+8=10. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate the exponent \\(x^x\\) before doing the multiplication",
        "At \\(x=2,\\) the second term is \\(2(2^2)\\)"
      ],
